# OSV acquisition policy verification — 2026-11-16

Current status: Ox and central v3 implemented, installed-source hashes confirmed,
and source review completed. Governance public-copy checks passed 6/6 (373.059s).
Independent bounded criteria OSV-01..05 are supported as recorded below; final
validator confirmation is recorded in validation.md. Broad scanner/product acceptance
is unchanged.

## Authorized outcome and changes

The single OSV validity interval is <=12h since successful acquisition, owned by
the central Toolbox. Scans do not renew it. Ox no longer rejects a valid acquired
base because the upstream object's publication exceeds 24h. Identity, provenance,
report completeness and findings gates remain. Trivy/Grype retain 120h and existing
OSV advisory exceptions are untouched.

Ox changes: scripts/lib/backends.sh validates provenance for both OSV/Trivy but
applies upstream age only to Trivy; scripts/config/automation.json removes OSV's
86400-second limit. The default 86400 in the helper is also removed. Focused tests
cover old upstream sources, identity/provenance errors, preserved Trivy rejection,
and real Ox report classification through fake transport.

Central implemented successor: publish successful download acquired_at atomically with the
snapshot identity in current.json, including manual and identical-content updates.
Reuse immutable snapshots and preserve old data for readers. Validate before
publication; preserve state on failed acquisition. Remove file mtime as a clock.
Migrate a matching known legacy receipt with its exact timestamp, preserving
<=12h reuse. Explicit native OSV maintenance is rejected before effects with
update-db guidance, because generic native commands cannot attest acquisition.

