## Policy/documentation audit and disposition

Reviewed and updated: scripts/README.md (single clock, lifecycle, migration and
failure semantics), docs/decisions/osv-acquisition-validity.md (current authority),
scanner-toolbox-ownership.md and scripts-toolbox-native.md (explicit historical
supersession notices), sdd/project.md, scripts-toolbox-native/spec/plan/tasks and
scripts-toolchain-config/spec/plan/tasks. Prior 24h prose in dated decisions/plans
remains historical with an explicit current successor; it is not current policy.

Reviewed unchanged: README.md delegates scanner instructions to scripts/README.md;
docs/constitution.md and docs/architecture/context.md do not define OSV clocks or
need product changes. scripts/security/SOURCES.md has only historical preparation
references. dependency-hygiene tasks/convergence describe historical expired-data
observations; their advisory exceptions and native config bytes remain unchanged.
Trivy/grype/osv-scanner native policies have no task diff. Historical validation
logs, snapshots and evidence keep original timestamps/hashes.

Reviewed static guards cover the three changed test files. Only hashes tied to
independently inspected new inputs were updated; no baseline/rule/severity was
removed. Content-sensitive governance requires a new successor, not rewriting an
old reviewed hash or accepting arbitrary live bytes.

Bound current observations in configuration-cohesion AC-16, terminal-progress
AC-01..06 and history-scanner-correction AC-03 referenced the changed Ox input
bundle. Their previous evidence.json/converge.md bytes are retained under prior/;
they now show UNVERIFIED and retain historical observations without hash renewal.
Those broader criteria require their own reexamination and are not accepted by
the OSV tests. The existing scanner features retain their undecided broad gates.

## Independent acceptance

OSV-01..05 criteria/methods and scope are defined in plan.md. Final criterion
verdicts are recorded in validation.md. Installed central files match all six v3 after hashes;
central/apply-journal.json records the completed publication, with exact command
executor/dispatch attribution unresolved as described in review.md. Independent
validation ran 29 OSV +33 native tests on those installed sources, all passing. No full scanner run, real
download, native Docker qualification, commit or publication was performed here.
Offline tests do not establish network availability, hardware crash durability or
broader current scanner readiness. Central and Ox source changes are separate
from acceptance of the entire application or complete automation scope.

## Central offline evidence and history

central/ contains the final reviewed patch, before/after manifest, command records,
fixture logs and application journal. Final candidate checks passed 29 OSV, 17
configuration and 33 native tests. The new OSV suite run against predecessor
implementation failed (7 failures and 21 API/contract errors), as expected; this
is a regression signal, not proof that every individual test detects a behavioral
bug. Applicator fixture succeeded; drift, repeat application and symlink inputs
were rejected with exit 2. Baseline attempts and earlier review findings remain
historical; their initial success did not validate the later-discovered consumers.
No operational database snapshots/cache were deleted or downloaded during this work.

The final governance fixture guard changes only one source SHA; its old and new
configuration identities are in final-config-review.json. Earlier Ox suite bindings
stay in ox-test-inputs.json and are not silently rewritten. The final validator
observed central toolbox.json SHA256
f207ad785164f8fee1db3b2a26ebe3de0e7ee93a919d6650783a732ce4710776,
with data.osv_refresh_hours = 12. This unchanged central configuration supplements
the six-file implementation manifest. Offline tests use literal 43200 boundaries
as the independent expected interval; filesystem locks and atomic rename are real,
while HTTP and Docker effects are controlled test doubles.

Final read-only static guard audit compared all 32 source/policy entries in
scripts/config/automation.json with current SHA256: zero mismatches. This checks
content bindings only and does not replace native scanner execution.

