| OSV-03 | APPROVED | Same OSV suite plus 33 native tests: manual/identical acquisition, failures, early maintenance rejection |
| OSV-04 | APPROVED | Real temporary filesystem locks/atomic pointer replacement, prior snapshot retention, concurrency and failed commit tests |
| OSV-05 | APPROVED | Independent source/document review, exact authenticated succession, 32 focused governance +6 public-copy tests, check-ox PASS |

These are manual bounded results, not a new schema-2 approval of the broad scanner
features. Review and validation contexts are independent of the implementation.
Changed dependent historical envelopes are preserved and remain UNVERIFIED; no
prior hashes are recomputed to imply rerunning their original checks. Complete
scanner operation, real acquisition/network behavior and broad Docker qualification
remain outside this authorized offline verification. No commit/publication occurred.

Documentation closure reviewed the current README/ADRs/project/spec/plan/tasks and
historical authority chain. The new registry normalizes only the two exact reviewed
README/project successors and retains authenticated preimages, rather than changing
an old registry or granting acceptance to unknown appended bytes. Native/external
source docs now explain clock ownership and migration; unrelated product architecture,
Trivy/Grype and advisory configs were inspected and left unchanged.
